AMDMIGraphX (pinned tag rocm-6.4.4): accumulate fp16 GEMMs in fp32 on gfx803.

WHY
---
MIGraphX decides per device whether an fp16 GEMM computes in fp32
(get_compute_fp32_flag, src/targets/gpu/rocblas.cpp). The flag is true only for
gfx908 and later gfx9 parts. When it is false the GEMM's compute type equals its
output type (gemm_impl.cpp), so an fp16 GEMM calls rocBLAS with an fp16 compute
type and runs the Type_HH Tensile kernels, which sum the whole K dimension in
fp16. gfx803 takes that path, and gets nothing for it: it has no packed fp16
arithmetic, so the fp16-compute kernels are not faster than the Type_HH_HPA
kernels, which accumulate in fp32. Both families ship in the gfx803 Tensile
libraries. With fp16 accumulation the rounding error of a GEMM grows with K
(transformer projections have K of 1024 to 5120), while the fp32-accumulate
kernels keep it near the fp16 output rounding. The fp32 route is also the one
the rest of this stack uses and has validated for fp16 GEMMs.

WHAT
----
Make get_compute_fp32_flag return true for gfx803 as well, so fp16 and bf16
GEMMs use an fp32 compute type with fp32 alpha and beta, exactly as on gfx908 and
later. The marker GFX803_GEMM_COMPUTE_FP32 sits once in rocblas.cpp.

VERIFICATION (RX 590, gfx803, image built with this patch): tools/correctness-suite/pytorch/migraphx_check.py runs fp16
dot programs with K = 4096 and 2048 through the gpu target against float64 from the same fp16 inputs. Without the patch
the relative L2 error is 6.6e-3 to 9.6e-3 (fp16 accumulation); with it 2.1e-4, below the fp16 output rounding.

diff --git a/src/targets/gpu/rocblas.cpp b/src/targets/gpu/rocblas.cpp
index 8c06ad5..7b7758e 100644
--- a/src/targets/gpu/rocblas.cpp
+++ b/src/targets/gpu/rocblas.cpp
@@ -51,7 +51,11 @@ rocblas_handle_ptr create_rocblas_handle_ptr(hipStream_t s)
 bool get_compute_fp32_flag()
 {
     const auto device_name = trim(split_string(get_device_name(), ':').front());
-    return (starts_with(device_name, "gfx9") and device_name >= "gfx908");
+    // GFX803_GEMM_COMPUTE_FP32: gfx803 has no packed fp16 arithmetic, so rocBLAS's fp16-compute GEMMs
+    // (Type_HH) gain no speed there and accumulate the whole K sum in fp16, while the fp32-accumulate
+    // kernels (Type_HH_HPA) keep the rounding error independent of K.
+    return (starts_with(device_name, "gfx9") and device_name >= "gfx908") or
+           device_name == "gfx803";
 }
 
 bool rocblas_fp8_available()
